# 3. Use one real document repository architecture

The project is currently frontend-only. Do not store document bodies, uploaded binaries, or complete version snapshots in localStorage.

Continue using `useDocumentRegistry` for lightweight document metadata.

Continue using `useDocumentVersionRegistry` for lightweight version metadata.

Store actual document content and uploaded file blobs in IndexedDB.

Add a small IndexedDB library such as Dexie.

Create:

- `src/app/services/types/documents.ts`
- `src/app/services/repositories/documentRepository.ts`
- `src/app/services/repositories/localDocumentRepository.ts`
- `src/app/services/repositories/apiDocumentRepository.ts`
- `src/app/services/repositories/documentContentStore.ts`
- `src/app/services/endpoints/documents.ts`

Create one repository contract such as:

```ts
interface DocumentRepository {
  getDocument(documentId: string): Promise<BoardDocument | null>;
  createDocument(input: CreateDocumentInput): Promise<BoardDocument>;
  updateDocument(documentId: string, patch: Partial<BoardDocument>): Promise<BoardDocument>;

  saveOriginalFile(documentId: string, file: File): Promise<string>;
  getOriginalFile(documentId: string): Promise<Blob | null>;

  getContent(documentId: string): Promise<DocumentContent | null>;
  saveContent(documentId: string, content: DocumentContent): Promise<void>;

  listVersions(documentId: string): Promise<DocumentVersion[]>;
  createVersion(input: CreateDocumentVersionInput): Promise<DocumentVersion>;
  restoreVersion(documentId: string, versionId: string): Promise<DocumentVersion>;

  listComments(documentId: string): Promise<DocumentCommentThread[]>;
  addComment(input: CreateDocumentCommentInput): Promise<DocumentCommentThread>;
  updateComment(threadId: string, patch: Partial<DocumentCommentThread>): Promise<void>;

  listAccess(documentId: string): Promise<DocumentAccessGrant[]>;
  updateAccess(documentId: string, grants: DocumentAccessGrant[]): Promise<void>;

  listApprovals(documentId: string): Promise<DocumentApproval[]>;
  updateApproval(input: UpdateDocumentApprovalInput): Promise<void>;
}